  "comment": "wb-1xvp.4 (RF-GRAPH-POLICY-MACHINE-CONTROL-R3; the hk9l/5jha roster pattern), extended by wb-qxdr (the 1xvp.4 PREP F1 follow-up): the OUT-OF-FILE anchor of test/workbench-gp-fallback-census.test.ts. rows: every judged row of test/helpers/gp-fallback-census.ts in census order (TOUCHPOINTS, CLEAN, RESIDUALS, FAMILIES, UNUSABLE, MUTANTS, PAIRING_CASES, WALKS) - table, id, label, the SHA-256 of each pin as written (a source; a fake seam with its reason and code; a mutant's shape, edits and expected rules; a pairing case's pairings, files and expected rules; a walk case's planted tree and its expected listing or refusal) and the registered test. tests: every test the census file registers, in order. residuals: the named residual families and their pinned quiet rows. Written from the rows as measured at the cut; the census judges its tables, its registered tests (vitest task tree, run modes) and its residual families against this file at test time, in order and both ways.",
